# =============================================================================
# Prionex CRM Frontend - STAND Environment Variables (template)
# =============================================================================
# Use with: docker-compose.stand.yml (Story 4.1's parameterized stand file).
# docker-compose.server.yml is the LEGACY stand's file and is untouched by
# this template - do not point this file at it.
#
# Copy this file to the stand's own .env (e.g.
# ~/crm-prionex/fe-prionex-dev/.env) and replace every <CHANGE_ME> below.
#
# EVERY placeholder is deliberately INVALID, not merely wrong. The angle
# brackets are the mechanism: "<" and ">" are illegal in a compose project
# name, a container name, a port and an image reference, so a template copied
# unedited refuses on the FIRST variable it reaches and keeps refusing until
# all five are real. This is by design, and it was a review finding: a bare
# CHANGE_ME is a VALID Docker container name, so the earlier version of this
# file would start a stand with a container literally called CHANGE_ME, and
# nothing downstream would have caught it.
#
# How each one fails if left unedited (verified, compose v5.3.0):
#   COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME  config refuses - invalid project name
#   CONTAINER_NAME        up refuses     - Invalid container name, only
#                                          [a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_.-] allowed
#   FRONTEND_PORT         config refuses - invalid hostPort
#   DOCKER_IMAGE          up refuses     - invalid reference format
#   FRONTEND_NETWORK      up refuses     - network declared as external,
#                                          but could not be found
#
# There is no default for any of these in docker-compose.stand.yml. A MISSING
# value refuses with a message naming the variable. A WRONG-BUT-VALID value is
# NOT caught by anything - see FRONTEND_NETWORK below, where that failure is
# also silent.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME - the compose project name for this stand.
# Must be unique per stand on the host, e.g. fe-prionex-dev, fe-prionex-preprod.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=<CHANGE_ME>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTAINER_NAME - the container name for this stand.
# Must be unique per stand, and must NEVER be "fe-prionex" - CD.yml:201
# force-removes that exact literal name on every legacy deploy. `docker rm -f`
# is name-based and project-independent (measured in Story 4.1, Task 5.4): it
# crosses compose projects, so reusing the name means a legacy deploy removes
# THIS stand's container.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONTAINER_NAME=<CHANGE_ME>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND_PORT - the host-side published port. The container side is fixed at
# 80 and is not configurable here (baked into the image: nginx.conf `listen 80`,
# Dockerfile.prod `EXPOSE 80`).
#
# Port allocations on s1 - the two you must NOT take are named explicitly,
# because a warning you have to decode is a warning that gets misread:
#   8080  TAKEN - the legacy stand. Untouched, and staying that way (NFR5).
#   8081  TAKEN - NOT by a stand. `docker-proxy` binds 127.0.0.1:8081 for
#                 vm-cadvisor. FR25 once called this a "permanent allocation"
#                 for PRE-PROD on the strength of a port census run from the
#                 artifacts instead of by SSH; it was measured taken on
#                 2026-08-15 and FR25 was amended. Taking it collides with an
#                 unrelated system service, not with another stand.
#   8082  new DEV stand (Story 4.2)
#   8083  PRE-PROD (Story 5.2) - the amended value
#   PROD on s10 is measured there by Story 6.10, not listed here.
#
# Never copy a port from another stand's .env.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FRONTEND_PORT=<CHANGE_ME>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOCKER_IMAGE - the full image reference including tag. There is no default
# and none is coming: ":latest" is CANCELLED (D20 section 4) and is never
# published by the pipeline (build.yml sets PUSH_LATEST=false).
#
# Tag shape is one of:
#   sha-<12hex>-<env>
#   <sanitized-branch>-<env>
# where env is one of: dev, preprod, prod.
#
# Example shape only, not a working value:
#   git.crm-prionex.com/crm/fe-prionex:sha-0123456789ab-dev
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DOCKER_IMAGE=<CHANGE_ME>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND_NETWORK - the pre-existing external network this stand attaches to.
#
# THIS IS THE ONE AXIS WHERE A WRONG VALUE FAILS SILENTLY, and no guard can
# catch it. nginx uses a lazy-resolving variable upstream for Kong, so the
# container starts and serves its static assets whether or not the backend
# resolves; the healthcheck probes 127.0.0.1:80 - itself - and proves nothing
# about the backend. Story 4.1 Task 6.2 demonstrated a stand on a backend-less
# network reporting `healthy` and serving 200 while `crm-kong-gateway` did not
# resolve at all.
#
# The network must ALREADY EXIST before this stand is brought up - it is
# created by the corresponding api-prionex stack. This compose file never
# creates it, and no deploy path may either: `external: true` refusing to start
# is the ONLY loud failure available on this axis, and auto-creating the
# network converts that refusal into an empty, backend-less network that comes
# up happily (CD.yml:185 is exactly this anti-pattern).
#
# After bringing a stand up, VERIFY the backend from inside the container -
# "it started" is not evidence:
#     docker exec <container> getent hosts crm-kong-gateway
# An empty result is a STOP. It is NOT a reason to fall back to crm-network.
#
# api-prionex network names, by stand:
#   crm-dev-network      - new DEV stand
#   crm-preprod-network  - PRE-PROD stand
#   crm-prod-network     - PROD stand
#   crm-network          - legacy stand ONLY. Attaching a new stand here
#                          silently reattaches it to the legacy backend.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FRONTEND_NETWORK=<CHANGE_ME>
